## Effective ordering of validation & side-effects for `POST /api/owners`

1. Framework Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@Valid`) → 400 via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`. (postcode & sharesHousehold have no bean constraints.)
2. `addressNormalizer.normalize` (mutates address)
3. `ownerRequestValidator` (required fields) → 400
4. `postcodeValidator` → 400
5. `cityOwnerLimitValidator` (DB count) → 409
6. `registrationDateValidator` (future date) → 400
7. `dailyOwnerLimitValidator` (DB count) → 429
8. `telephoneNormalizer.normalize` (mutates telephone) → 400
9. `emailNormalizer.normalize` (mutates email) → 400
10. `disposableEmailDomainValidator` → 400
11. `ownerMapper.toOwner` (id & pets ignored)
12. `householdIdGenerator.generate` → set householdId
13. if `sharesHousehold`: clear possibleDuplicate flags; else `duplicateOwnerValidator` (409) + `possibleDuplicateDetector`
14. `customerCodeGenerator.generate` → set customerCode
15. `countNamesakes` → set namesakeCount
16. `householdSizeCalculator.size` → set householdSize
17. `clinicService.saveOwner` → `ownerRepository.save` → JPA `persist` → **`Owner.@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate()`** defaults/business-day-adjusts registrationDate
18. `ownerAuditLogger.created` (SLF4J)
19. build `OwnerDto` (+ `bulkSignupWarningEvaluator`), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 CREATED**

A note worth your analysis: derived fields computed in steps 12-18 read `registrationDate` before the `@PrePersist` in step 17 finalizes it, so any value derived from the registration date pre-save can diverge from what is persisted.
